.TH "PERCH" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch \- a small IMAP mailbox service backed by mxRaven
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch [OPTIONS] COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
perch runs a local IMAP server and authenticated submission endpoint, backed by mxRaven for inbound MX, outbound delivery, SPF/DKIM/DMARC, IP reputation, and spam filtering.
.PP
Messages are stored in SQLite or offloaded to S3. The same binary provides administrative commands and a scriptable mail client for IMAP and SMTP.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Run perch help <command> or see the per\-command manpages for details.
.IP \(bu 2
The default configuration path is $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/perch/perch.yaml.
.IP \(bu 2
perch does not need a public IP, port forwarding, or inbound SMTP ports.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.TP
.B \-\-version, \-v
print the version
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
create a local configuration and optional first account
.TP
.B setup
create the mxRaven domain, listeners, keys, and routes
.TP
.B serve
run IMAP, submission, and the notification consumer
.TP
.B account
add, list, password, disable, enable, or delete accounts
.TP
.B alias
manage address aliases and catch\-all domains
.TP
.B mailbox
list mailboxes for an account
.TP
.B mail
list, search, fetch, and send mail
.TP
.B doctor
check the database, TLS, S3, and mxRaven connectivity
.TP
.B backup
write a consistent SQLite backup
.TP
.B reconcile
force one S3 bucket reconciliation pass
.TP
.B gc
remove orphan blobs, old dead letters, and S3 tombstones
.TP
.B outbound
list submitted messages and delivery status
.TP
.B version
print the version
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch setup \-\-workspace my\-workspace \-\-domain example.com \-\-hostname localhost

perch account add \-\-email you@example.com

perch serve \-\-config ~/.local/share/perch/perch.yaml

perch mail list \-\-server 127.0.0.1:1143 \-\-plaintext \-\-username you@example.com
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PERCH_CONFIG
path to perch.yaml
.TP
.B PERCH_DATA_DIR
override data_dir
.TP
.B PERCH_HOSTNAME
override hostname
.TP
.B PERCH_IMAP_USER
default account username for perch mail
.TP
.B PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD
account password for perch mail
.TP
.B PERCH_S3_SECRET_KEY
S3 secret when storage.s3.secret_key_env selects it
.TP
.B PERCH_MXRAVEN_KEY_SECRET
mxRaven MTA listener secret
.TP
.B PERCH_MXRAVEN_SUBMISSION_KEY_SECRET
mxRaven submission listener secret
.TP
.B MXRAVEN_API_TOKEN
legacy control\-plane token used by perch setup
.TP
.B MXRAVEN_ISSUER
mxRaven identity issuer URL
.TP
.B MXRAVEN_DASHBOARD_URL
mxRaven dashboard URL used for connected\-app approval
.TP
.B MXRAVEN_CLIENT_ID
registered perch connected\-app client ID
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/perch/perch.yaml
Default configuration file ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/perch/perch.yaml).
.TP
.B ~/.config/perch/perch.db
Default SQLite database when data_dir is not overridden.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime or usage error.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\-account\fR(1), \fBperch\-alias\fR(1), \fBperch\-backup\fR(1), \fBperch\-doctor\fR(1), \fBperch\-gc\fR(1), \fBperch\-init\fR(1), \fBperch\-mail\fR(1), \fBperch\-mailbox\fR(1), \fBperch\-outbound\fR(1), \fBperch\-reconcile\fR(1), \fBperch\-serve\fR(1), \fBperch\-setup\fR(1), \fBperch\-version\fR(1)
